# @epistemologic/liquid/extraction — the OPERATIONAL subspecies
# under @epistemologic/liquid theory (Mara THIS-tick species-decl
# at `shards/epistemologic/liquid.mirror`). Recovers refinement
# predicates from doc-claim narrative at the doc-code seam per
# Rondon-Kawaguchi-Jhala 2008 + Vazou et al 2014.
#
# === Migration from @epistemologic/liquid_extraction ===
#
# This file MIGRATED from `shards/epistemologic/liquid_extraction.
# mirror` (Mara 2026-07-06, `3283de4` TICK 2 RATIFY) per Alex
# 2026-07-17 arbitration of Taut Q-C from `docs/audits/2026-07-17-
# taut-liquid-epistemologic-silicon-scout.md` (Taut `b8c453f`,
# +940 LOC): extraction is a SUBSPECIES UNDER liquid theory, NOT
# a peer of theory. Delightfully-boring name: `@epistemologic/
# liquid/extraction` reads as "the extraction subspecies of the
# liquid theory family." The prior sibling-at-logical-altitude
# framing was substrate-drift; the ratified three-altitude
# structure places theory ABOVE operation.
#
# Migration cascade at this tick:
#   1. `shards/epistemologic/liquid.mirror` (Mara THIS-tick, cc816f9)
#      lands the theory species-decl one altitude UP.
#   2. THIS file lands as the operational subspecies UNDER theory
#      at `shards/epistemologic/liquid/extraction.mirror`; prism
#      decl renamed `@epistemologic/liquid_extraction` →
#      `@epistemologic/liquid/extraction`.
#   3. Consumer refs updated: `bootstrap/tests/liquid_extraction_
#      shard.rs` path + prism-name assertions synced.
#
# Historical Seam Phase D ratification chain PRESERVED as-is: the
# TICK 2 `3283de4` ratification at `docs/audits/2026-07-06-seam-
# phase-d-arc-3-tick-2-liquid-extraction.md` remains valid history;
# the ratified shape moves under liquid theory without invalidating
# what was ratified.
#
# === Sibling relationship to @docblock ===
#
# @docblock (family-root landed TICK 1 at `5c0f5ba`) declares the
# doc-claim carrier surface: `doc_claim`, `claim_kind`, `docblock`,
# `audit_boundary`, `docblock_verdict`, plus the routing actions
# (`extract_claims`, `project`, `audit_docblock`, `docblock_well_
# audited`). @epistemologic/liquid/extraction retains the sibling
# family-root relationship @epistemologic/liquid_extraction
# originally landed: the two families operate at COUPLED altitudes
# on the same doc-claim operator (per recognition #59 the doc-
# claim operator is altitude-portable); @docblock names the
# carrier; extraction names the operational lowering.
#
# The `in @docblock` import below the seam grounds the sibling
# relationship at the substrate level: this shard's `extractor_
# input` specializes @docblock's `doc_claim`. Bilateral
# discipline per recognition #53 sixth-instance closes the two-
# way coupling: @docblock's `extract_claims` action returns
# claims; this shard's `extract_predicate` lifts each claim to a
# liquid predicate.
#
# === Logical altitude per Mara §3 four-altitude structure ===
#
# Mara's compiler-fit doc §3 names four altitudes on the same
# doc-claim operator, all altitude-portable per recognition #59:
#
# - linguistic — @epistemologic/property/docblock_{grounded,
#   coherent,no_extraction_pattern} audit docblock language
#   before it enters the type system. LANDED at Arc-3 sub-arc A
#   close 2026-07-06.
# - logical — THIS SHARD (post-migration). Lowers doc claims to
#   liquid predicates per Rondon-Kawaguchi-Jhala 2008 + Vazou et
#   al 2014. Under the ratified three-altitude structure,
#   extraction is the operational lowering; @epistemologic/
#   liquid (theory species) is the refinement-theory the
#   lowering targets. The substrate's `@projection.preview`
#   verdict IS the decidable fragment; the extractor produces
#   its input. Extractor body forward-promised per
#   `[[feedback-craft-not-deliver]]`.
# - temporal — the projection surface at `63bdecc` projects doc
#   claims forward k=3 substrate ticks as typed carriers landed
#   back in the doc's own observation side (below `---`).
# - publishable — docblock claims across `shards/` aggregate into
#   case-study crystals at systemic.engineering.
#
# The logical altitude sits BETWEEN linguistic (audit surface at
# language altitude) and temporal (projection surface at
# recognition-candidate altitude). It is the altitude at which
# linguistic material becomes formally decidable — the substrate's
# liquid-refinement fragment per Rondon-Kawaguchi-Jhala + Vazou.
# Named "logical" per Mara §3 because the operator here is proof-
# theoretic (predicates on data) as opposed to linguistic
# (narrative parse) or temporal (forward-projection).
#
# === Property/fracture bilateral pattern (#53 sixth-instance) ===
#
# Per recognition #53 the substrate has a bilateral pattern:
# declarative property at `@epistemologic/property/<predicate>` +
# operational fracture body at `@kintsugi/fracture/<predicate>`,
# bridged by the kintsugi loop. Fifth instance landed at
# `@kintsugi/surface` + `@epistemologic/cybernetic/coherence-
# parametric.ashby_variety_match` (2026-07-03 `e910dd6`). The
# SIXTH FAMILY at the doc-claim altitude is grounded at TICK 1's
# @docblock landing; each of the three property/fracture pairs
# (grounded, coherent, no_extraction_pattern) is a #53-shaped
# bilateral instance landed at Arc-3 sub-arc A close 2026-07-06.
#
# This shard's `liquid_extraction_sound` bilateral predicate
# carries the operational half of the extractor's discipline:
# the extractor is sound when its lowered predicate soundly
# reflects the doc claim's substrate-observable content.
# Fracture-side body forward-promised per `[[feedback-craft-not-
# deliver]]`.
#
# === Path-namespace property ===
#
# This file at `shards/epistemologic/liquid/extraction.mirror`
# declares `@epistemologic/liquid/extraction` at species-depth 2
# under @epistemologic (@epistemologic → @epistemologic/liquid →
# @epistemologic/liquid/extraction) per @epistemologic/pact/
# path_matches_namespace. The depth matches the property-family
# bilateral pattern the substrate uses at `@epistemologic/
# property/*` and `@epistemologic/cybernetic/*`: extraction is
# an epistemologic-liquid discipline (the substrate is checking
# what liquid-refinement content it can lower from a doc claim),
# NOT a doc-claim carrier (that lives at @docblock).
#
# === Circular-reflexive self-audit ===
#
# The operator must audit its own audit at depth=3 per `63bdecc`
# §6. This shard's own docblock must survive `audit_docblock
# (this_docblock, depth=3)` and `liquid_extraction_sound
# (extract_claims(this_docblock), verdict)` per the sibling
# coupling. At this tick, the extractor's body is forward-
# promised, so the self-audit verdict at logical altitude is
# `unextractable` — the honest answer given no extractor is
# landed. Promotion of `liquid_extraction_sound` to a decidable
# verdict awaits the extractor body and property/fracture
# bilateral trio.
#
# === Composed-over ===
#
# - `shards/epistemologic/liquid.mirror` (Mara THIS-tick, cc816f9)
#   — the theory species-decl this subspecies operationally
#   instantiates. `extract_predicate` returns a
#   refinement_predicate the theory defines; `extraction_verdict`
#   specializes the theory's liquid_verdict.
# - `shards/docblock.mirror` (`5c0f5ba` TICK 1 RATIFY) — the
#   doc-claim carrier this subspecies extracts from.
# - `docs/math/liquid-types/README.md` (Mara 2026-07-05) §2 the
#   `extract` operator this subspecies discharges.
# - `docs/specs/doc-code-seam-shards.md` §2 — the RED test targets.
#
# === Substrate decisions ===
#
# [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]] — subspecies is
#   shard-decl.
# [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]] — `prism
#   @epistemologic/liquid/extraction` declares the subspecies IS
#   a prism.
# [[architecture-property-fracture-bilateral]] — `liquid_
#   extraction_sound` is the #53-shaped bilateral this
#   subspecies carries at logical altitude.
# [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]] — the extraction
#   discipline landed 2026-07-06; this tick MOVES it under
#   liquid theory per Q-C ratification; ZERO new mint.
# [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]] — extractor + bilateral bodies
#   remain forward-promised.
# [[feedback-no-rust-extension-shortcut]] — migration is shard-
#   move + prism-rename + consumer-ref sync; ZERO Rust.

---

in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @kintsugi
in @epistemologic
in @epistemologic/property
in @epistemologic/liquid
in @docblock

prism @epistemologic/liquid/extraction {
  focus liquid_extraction
  project liquid_extraction
  split liquid_extraction
  shift liquid_extraction
  settle liquid_extraction
}

# === extractor_input — one doc_claim as extraction input (spec §2) ===
#
# Per Mara spec §2: the extractor input is exactly a @docblock-side
# `doc_claim`. Newtyped per `[[feedback-no-bare-types]]`; the alias
# to `doc_claim` names the sibling coupling at the type level.
type extractor_input = doc_claim

# === predicate_shape — extractor output carrier (spec §2) ===
#
# Per Mara spec §2: the extractor's output is a `splinter(@epistemo-
# logic/property/ast)` fragment carried at ref shape per the
# substrate's content-addressing discipline. Newtyped per
# `[[feedback-no-bare-types]]` so the extraction output is not
# confused with any other ref-shape at this altitude. Under the
# ratified three-altitude structure, this ref IS an instance of
# the theory's refinement_predicate at
# `shards/epistemologic/liquid.mirror`.
type predicate_shape = ref

# === extraction_verdict — four variants (spec §2) ===
#
# Per Mara spec §2: the four-verdict output specializes the
# `@projection.preview` verdict machinery to the liquid-extraction
# altitude. Under the ratified three-altitude structure, this
# variant set is a specialization of the theory's liquid_verdict at
# `shards/epistemologic/liquid.mirror`.
#
# `satisfiable` — extractor lowered the claim to a liquid
# predicate the substrate can decide; `unsatisfiable` — lowered but
# the predicate is provably false against the substrate below;
# `partial` — extractor lowered part of the claim (composite
# narrative with mixed groundable + non-groundable clauses);
# `unextractable` — extractor could not lower the claim at all
# (natural language beyond the liquid fragment; no predicate shape
# recoverable). Grounds Rondon-Kawaguchi-Jhala 2008 decidability
# fragment + Vazou et al 2014 refinement discipline at doc-claim
# altitude.
type extraction_verdict =
  | satisfiable
  | unsatisfiable
  | partial
  | unextractable

# === extract_predicate — extractor_input → ref (spec §2) ===
#
# Per Mara spec §2: lowers a doc_claim to a `splinter(@epistemologic/
# property/ast)` fragment carrying the liquid predicate. Output is
# a ref carrying the splinter(ast) discipline per
# `[[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]`. Body forward-promised
# per `[[feedback-craft-not-deliver]]`; discharge via splinter(ast)
# at the property altitude when the extractor lands.
extract_predicate(i: extractor_input) -> ref { \ }

# === liquid_extraction_sound — bilateral predicate (spec §2) ===
#
# Per Mara spec §2 the #53-family bilateral: the extractor is sound
# when its lowered predicate soundly reflects the doc claim's
# substrate-observable content. Carries the declarative-side
# property; the operational-side fracture body lands with the
# property/fracture bilateral pairs at Arc-3 sub-arc A close
# 2026-07-06. Body forward-promised — discharge via
# `splinter(@epistemologic/property/ast)` against the extractor's
# output AST fragment when the extractor body lands.
liquid_extraction_sound(i: extractor_input, v: extraction_verdict) -> verdict { \ }

out @epistemologic/liquid/extraction
out extractor_input
out predicate_shape
out extraction_verdict
out extract_predicate
out liquid_extraction_sound
